{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+ & Gram-, Antibiofilm", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "Unknown", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "APD analysis reveals that the sequence of this peptide most resembles (42.8% similarity) Pleurain-B1. Mol Wt 1390.6; mol formula: C63H99N21O15S0. Active against S. aureus ATCC 25923, S. aureus ATCC 6538, S. epidermidis ATCC 35984, and P. aeruginosa ATCC 15442 (MIC 12.5 mg/ml). It also inhibits biofilm formation of both S. aureus, S. epidermidis and P. aeruginosa. At the MIC, the peptide was not hemolytic. Provided by Luigi Inguglia and Vincenzo Arizza.", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "23800329", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "AMB Express. 2013 Jun 24;3(1):35. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP02622", "source_id": "AP02622", "source_numeric_id": "02622", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP02622", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "Immune mediators of sea-cucumber Holothuria tubulosa (Echinodermata) as source of novel antimicrobial and anti-staphylococcal biofilm agents", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
